# B3 WP-B review: a paste typed on a client under synchronize-panes. The text is copied as is; the paste markers are keys, so each pane gets them only if it turned bracketed paste on itself (pane 1 and 3 did, pane 2 did not), whatever the active pane asked for.
$ new-session -d -s main -x 60 -y 15 "printf '\\033[?2004h'; stty -echo; cat -v"
$ split-window -d -t main 'stty -echo; cat -v'
$ split-window -d -t main:.2 "printf '\\033[?2004h'; stty -echo; cat -v"
$ set-option -g status off
$ set-option -w -t main synchronize-panes on
$ run-shell 'sleep 1'
client 60x15 attach -t main
keys Escape [200~ hi Escape [201~ Enter
$ run-shell 'sleep 1'
$ capture-pane -p -t main:.1
$ capture-pane -p -t main:.2
$ capture-pane -p -t main:.3
$ select-pane -t main:.2
keys Escape [200~ yo Escape [201~ Enter
$ run-shell 'sleep 1'
$ capture-pane -p -t main:.1
$ capture-pane -p -t main:.2
$ capture-pane -p -t main:.3
